Round d1_r6 complete. Both deliverables written: `impl/d1_twiddle.c` and a new "Round d1_r6" section in `strategies/d1_twiddle.md`. Summary of what happened:

**Shipped changes**
1. **Latency-shaped chain map** (adopted from d1_prime r5, transfer confirmed by d1_batchlane r6): early-seeded reciprocal + Goldschmidt sqrt + additive 1e-100 floor, in all three of my map forms (AoS store, register-chain vmap, SoA split). Every one of my 14 graded chained cells improved **−3 to −10%** in interleaved node A/B (e.g. 4096 B=1 chain 11.45→10.73 µs, 16384 B=64 chain 57.8→54.3 µs, 32 B=512 chain 0.037→0.034 µs).
2. **Register-fused first stage pair extended to L=128** with pow2's batch-working-set gate: 128 B=1 m=1 0.113–0.126→0.105–0.110 µs (−6..−10%, now at/under MKL's r5 board 0.1044); B=512 correctly stays on the old path (fused lost 9% there).
3. **The huge-page arena (pow2 r5 / bluestein) was built, measured, and gated OFF**: on my engine it was a pure loss — +8–9% at 16384 B=1 m=1 in every variant (THP off, tables-out, skew shift), wash everywhere else. It ships behind `-DD1TW_ARENA=1` with the negative result recorded so nobody re-derives it.

**Correctness**: single-call rel L2 ≤ 3.9e-16 at 17 sizes + all graded batch shapes; all 14 graded chain gates PASS (worst 1.17e-11 vs 1e-10 tolerance, statistically unchanged from r5); 8 edge-path chains pass; output bitwise repeatable; official tryout.sh green. Slot lease released.

One-line close-out as requested:

